<title>FRANCE: Rain hits western France, more forecast at weekend.</title>
<headline>Rain hits western France, more forecast at weekend.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Light rain hit western France on Friday and more rain was expected to bring thirsty crops some relief over the next four days, a spokesman for the national meteorological service Meteo France said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a change in the weather pattern. Rain over the next four days will bring crops some relief although it will not be sufficient to make up for the water shortfall,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>On Friday morning it was raining lightly over Brittany with scattered showers heading to the north and the east.</p>
<p>Another rainy front was expected to hit Brittany on Saturday morning, he said.</p>
</text>
